{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790289994,"nonce":"q0VjTbQgAJo1aJcor8jjgOmgeis=","title":"Lua: the host's os and io functions do not compile for Windows","message":"`cargo check --target x86_64-pc-windows-msvc -p zyntax_lua` fails with 13 errors: `crates/zyntax_lua/src/host_os.rs` and `host_io.rs` call `libc::mkstemp`, `gmtime_r`, `localtime_r`, `mktime`, `strftime`, `WIFEXITED`/`WEXITSTATUS`/`WIFSIGNALED`/`WTERMSIG`, `std::os::fd::FromRawFd` and `std::os::unix::process::ExitStatusExt`, none of which exist for Windows. The Windows CI job has not reached this crate yet (it stopped earlier), so it would be the next compile failure there.\n\nFix: Windows implementations beside the Unix ones: `gmtime_s`/`localtime_s`; `_mktime64` and `strftime` declared from the UCRT; `os.tmpname` and `io.tmpfile` as a fresh file under the temporary directory (the latter delete-on-close); `io.popen` through `cmd /C`; and the status word of `system` and of a closed pipe is the exit code, as the reference reads it on Windows.\n\nNot verifiable without a Windows machine: runtime behaviour of these paths. Type-checked and clippy-clean for x86_64-pc-windows-msvc; the Unix paths are unchanged and the Lua conformance suite passes on macOS.","files":null}]}